-- title:
--   Genus of the Drinfeld curve function field is q(q-1)/2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $k$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over the Galois field `GaloisField q 2` of $q^2$ elements, so that $k$ contains $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$, and assume $k$ is algebraically closed. Let `CoordRing q k` be the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ k$ by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, the coordinate ring of the affine Drinfeld curve, and assume this quotient is an integral domain. Let `drinfeldFunctionField q k` be its fraction field. The assertion is that the genus of this function field over $k$, defined as the $k$-dimension $\mathrm{finrank}_k\,H^1(0)$ of the first cohomology space attached to the zero divisor in $\mathrm{Place}\ k\ F \to_{f} \mathbb{Z}$, equals $q(q-1)/2$. The right-hand side is computed in the natural numbers, with truncated subtraction and division; since $q \ge 2$ and $q(q-1)$ is even, it is the expected value.
--
--   This is the genus computation for the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^q y = 1$, whose function field over an algebraically closed field containing $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ has genus $q(q-1)/2$, the same value as for the Hermitian curve to which it is isomorphic. It is used in the curve's Abel–Jacobi and Jacobian point-count computations and in the analysis of the intertwining maps attached to cuspidal representations realised on the curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_genusFF_drinfeldFunctionField.lean

import Definitions.Def_DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace DrinfeldCurve

theorem genusFF_drinfeldFunctionField (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] (k : Type) [Field k] [Algebra (GaloisField q 2) k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] [IsDomain (CoordRing q k)] :
    AlgebraicCurve.genusFF k (drinfeldFunctionField q k) = q * (q - 1) / 2 := by sorry
